    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **287 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` field on the owner-creation response. When an owner is created, it is set to `'local'` if their city is the *single* most common city among existing owners at that moment, otherwise `'remote'`.\n\nChanges made, following the codebase's established pattern for derived owner fields (`namesakeCount`, `sharesHousehold`, etc.):\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `locality` string property to the `Owner` schema.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `locality` field (`@Column(name = \"locality\")`) with getter/setter.\n- **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `locality VARCHAR(20)` column.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 set `owner.setLocality(localityFor(owner.getCity()))` during `addOwner`, with a helper that:\n  - Groups existing owners by city (case-insensitive, whitespace-normalized via the existing `normalize`).\n  - Finds the max count; if exactly one city holds that max and it matches the new owner's city \u2192 `'local'`, else `'remote'`.\n  - Returns `'remote'` when there are no existing owners, the city is null, or the top city is a tie.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.java`** \u2014 added two tests: a new owner in Madison (the single most common seed city, 4 owners) \u2192 `local`; a new owner in Cardiff \u2192 `remote`.\n\nNote: I made `locality` a plain string rather than an OpenAPI enum on purpose \u2014 MapStruct maps the model String to a generated enum via `Enum.valueOf(...)` by constant *name*, which would fail for lowercase values like `local`/`remote`. A plain string maps cleanly and serializes exactly as the spec requires.",
